  CHANGELOG:
    V2.3  Label unification (TL_ prefix). No logic changes.
    V2.4  (2026-06-12) P5 Holiday module rebuilt as HolidayFlat_v3:
          - Iron Rule: flat (0 position) BEFORE the 05:00 close of
            the last night session preceding every market closure.
          - Old design (eve date >= 13:30) replaced: it missed the
            post-midnight tail (00:00-05:00 bars stamped with the
            next calendar date) and never blocked entries.
          - Array semantics changed: Holiday_Tail = last trading
            day + 1 calendar day (the tail-bar date stamp).
          - Date errors fixed: Labor Day added for every year;
            all three 2026 entries corrected vs official TAIFEX
            115-yr calendar; H2 2026 + 2027/1/1 added.
          - Header performance figures reflect the OLD module;
            re-backtest pending after deployment.
          - Fail-safe horizon guard: Registry_Valid_Until input.
            Beyond the last verified registry date the strategy
            blocks entries and flattens (TL_RegistryEnd) - future
            holidays beyond the published TAIFEX calendar are
            unknowable, so walking off the verified map must fail
            safe, not fail silent. 30-day red warning on chart.
    V2.5  (2026-06-12) P3 initial stop FROZEN at entry:
          - Old code recomputed the stop EVERY BAR from current
            45M ATR and Daily ATR, so the floor drifted with
            volatility during the trade (user observed the live
            stop shifting between reloads). Now computed once on
            the entry bar close and locked (v_SL_Locked pattern,
            same as L2 SL_Locked / S1 v_EntryATR).
          - MA55 trail (P4) still updates by design; the frozen
            initial stop is the floor it can never drop below.
          - No new inputs. No entry-logic change.
          - DEPLOYMENT: changes historical exits -> recalculated
            chart may disagree with a live open position. Deploy
            ONLY WHEN FLAT (see annotated doc deployment note).
    V2.6  (2026-06-12) P7 Stop Profit Guard, ported from L2
          (Trendbearish_V1 SECTION 12), user-directed:
          - Activation: CLOSE-based profit >= 250 pts. Peak profit
            (posbleProfit_Long) ratchets up only; lock floor =
            Entry + peak x 45 pct moves only in the profit
            direction and never disarms until flat.
          - Guarantees: an armed runner can never round-trip into
            a loss (floor > entry by construction); giveback from
            peak is capped at 55 pct.
          - Data basis (469-trade MFE audit): 83 trades reached
            +100pts yet closed negative (-1,520,200); MFE>=250
            trades gave back median 50 pct / P90 112 pct; Top-10
            endpoint giveback max only 28 pct -> 55 pct tolerance
            clears the fat tail with huge margin.
          - Integrated as a third floor in Final_Exit (single-stop
            architecture kept; L2 uses an order-priority chain
            instead - effect identical). New exit label TL_SP.
          - Optimistic-bound improvement +1.93M; path-level
            whipsaw cost invisible to MFE data -> MC9 A/B is the
            final arbiter. Deploy only when flat.
    V2.7  (2026-07-02) Plan A: SP threshold 250 -> 500.
          - Backtest (SP500 only): Net +3,938K (+22.5%), PF 1.484,
            MDD -461K, trades 451, win/loss 3.19x, avg +6001/trade.
          - TL_SP exits 68 -> 12; freed trades flow to TL_TP
            (103 -> 141), letting trends run longer.
          Plan C REJECTED after A/B test:
          - Re-entry after passive exit (TL_SL/TL_SP/TL_SL_Gap).
          - Hypothesis +2.1M looked attractive but MC9 path-level
            backtest (A+C combined, SP500) showed Net 3,018K vs
            Plan A alone 3,938K = -920K drag. 69 re-entry trades
            net negative. Re-entry positions hit SL at worse prices
            than original breakout entries.
          - Decision: Plan A only. Plan C code removed.
          - Deploy only when flat.
    V2.6+ (2026-06-18) P3b Immediate Stop Guard:
          - SetStopLoss = MC engine-level stop, active on the
            ENTRY BAR itself (no IOG dependency). Closes the
            structural 45-minute unprotected window between fill
            and first custom stop order (IOG=false -> script
            evaluates at bar close only).
          - Distance = same as P3 frozen SL. (V2.6+..V2.7 shipped
            MaxList of DISTANCES here = the LOOSER leg, a doc-
            propagated paraphrase bug fixed in V2.9 -> MinList.)
          - Called only when flat (MP<=0) -> freezes automatically
            when position established (same principle as V2.5
            Frozen SL via v_SL_Locked).
          - Does NOT replace P3/P4/P7 exit logic. Once custom
            stops tighten beyond SetStopLoss, engine picks the
            tighter level. SetStopLoss becomes dormant backup.
          - Deploy only when flat.
    V2.9  (2026-07-22) P3b leg-selection fix + explicit contract basis:
          - ROOT CAUSE (doc-propagated bug): P3 code freezes
            MaxList of the two stop PRICES = Entry - MinList of
            the two DISTANCES = the TIGHTER leg; the cap leg
            (Daily_Cap_Multiplier) exists to LIMIT the distance.
            The old header wrongly paraphrased this as "entry -
            MaxList(distances)"; V2.6+ P3b copied that formula
            shape, so the entry-bar engine stop took the LOOSER
            leg: 1.6-2.8x wider than design intent on every entry.
          - Forensics (1M-bar reconstruction of ATR45/DailyATR,
            456 trades, frozen-distance prediction error p90 =
            1 pt): tight leg = ATR leg at 99-100 pct of entries;
            12 same-bar deaths filled at the wide leg (-460 pts
            excess); 2 legacy winners (#66 2020-12, #95 2021-05)
            survived the entry bar only because of the wide leg
            (-584 pts if killed). Expected net impact approx
            -124 pts / 6.5y (excl. re-entry) = EV-neutral
            insurance fix. At 2026-07-22 volatility: wide leg
            736 pts vs intended 266 pts (2.77x) -> fix removes
            ~470 pts unintended entry-bar exposure per entry.
          - SetStopContract declared explicitly: SetStopLoss
            amount is per-CONTRACT, invariant to lot count.
            Without it (per-position default) a 2-lot live
            deployment halves the effective stop distance; with
            MinList that would fire at half the frozen distance
            (a new bug). 1-lot backtests identical either way.
          - Verifier fixed in the same commit: the old
            verify_l1_immediate_stop.py V-4 asserted the buggy
            MaxList shape -- the bug passed verification because
            the verifier encoded the bug. Now asserts MinList +
            SetStopContract semantics.
          - V2.8 number skipped (daily-loss-cap experiment,
            REJECTED and reverted 2026-07-22).
          - MC12 gate BEFORE MC9 deploy: V2.7 vs V2.9 trade-list
            diff must concentrate in <= 52 candidate trades and
            every diff must be explained. Deploy only when flat.
            GATE RESULT (2026-07-22): PASS. 65 diffs all explained
            (12/12 same-bar saves, 2/2 predicted kills, 7 borderline
            grazes, 6 chain re-entries). Net -36 pts / 6.5y, closed
            MDD unchanged at 2,038 pts.
    V2.9.1 (2026-07-22) Exit-label taxonomy fix (labels only, no logic):
          - User ruling: loss-stop labels may ONLY mark losing
            exits; profit-taking must use separate labels. Old
            routing broke this twice: TL_TP (trail) could fire
            below entry (#452 -444 pts, 2026-07-07), and
            TL_SL_Gap could fire above entry (SP-lock gap-downs).
          - New routing = leg x side-of-entry:
            loss side  : Stop Loss (P3b engine, entry bar only),
                         TL_SL (frozen stop), TL_SL_Gap (gap,
                         level < entry), TL_TSL (trail < entry)
            profit side: TL_TP (trail >= entry), TL_SP (SP lock),
                         TL_SP_Gap (gap, level >= entry)
          - Labels are assigned at order placement; a gap through
            the entry price can still fill a profit-labeled order
            at a small loss (documented edge, not an overlap).
          - Zero P&L impact by construction. Re-gate: MC12 rerun
            must show IDENTICAL numbers, labels redistributed.
    V3.0  (2026-07-23) IOG migration: tick-level strategy evaluation.
          - IntrabarOrderGeneration = true. Script evaluates on every
            Data1 tick instead of only at 45M bar close.
          - BarStatus(1) = 2 guards on: indicators, weekly filter,
            holiday/settlement detection, entry (Crosses Over), P3
            frozen SL lock, MDD visualizer. These run at bar close
            only, preserving V2.9.1 semantics.
          - P7 now tracks intrabar peaks in real-time. Threshold
            lowered 500 -> 200 pts (IOG makes lower viable).
          - P4 trail upgraded to uni-directional ratchet (v_Trail_High
            via MaxList, never descends). Old bi-directional breathing
            let the effective stop sag during pullbacks.
          - IntraBarPersist added to posbleProfit_Long, stopProfitPrice_L,
            v_Trail_High -- without it these reset to bar-open on each tick.
          - Gap detection moved from every-tick to BarStatus=2 (bar close
            indicator recalc can push stop above Close; BarStatus=0 was
            dead code -- pending stop fills before script at bar open).
          - Daily_ATR [1] fix: references previous completed daily bar.
          - Code restructured: MP + SetStop moved before BarStatus=2 guard
            around entry logic (no data dependency between groups).
          - Backtest requires Bar Magnifier (1 min minimum).
          - 33/33 adversarial audit tests PASS (2 rounds).
          - GATE: MC12 entry count must match V2.9.1 (same period/params).
            Deploy only when flat.
    V3.1  (2026-07-24) L1_c primary SL replacing ATR-based Layer 1:
          - Layer 1 (primary SL) now driven by L1_c: max close-to-
            close drawdown over the last 10 completed Daily bars
            (from Data2, computed at BarStatus(1)=2), multiplied
            by L1c_Ratio, with an optional Floor_Points minimum.
          - Layer 0 (ATR wall) preserved unchanged as hard cap:
            MinList(Current_ATR * SL_Multiplier,
                    Daily_ATR   * Daily_Cap_Multiplier).
          - Final SL distance = MinList(Layer 1, Layer 0). Locked
            at entry via v_Frozen_SL_dist_locked (freeze mechanism
            mirrors V2.5 principle, translated to distance space).
          - Bug-1 fix: fallback triggers on BOTH cold-start
            (v_L1c_ready = false, Data2 < 11 bars) AND L1_c = 0
            (10-day all-up regime). Fallback distance =
            Current_ATR * SL_Multiplier (V3.0-equivalent Layer 1).
            Prevents SL price from collapsing onto EntryPrice.
          - Layer 1b (behavioral tightening / dynamic SL modification
            post-entry) KILLED. See
            docs/research/L1_Layer1b_kill_summary_20260724.md:
            framework constraint + sealed-list + L33 principle.
          - Layer 2 (P7 T200 profit lock) UNCHANGED from V3.0.
          - Layer 3 (P4 MA55 trail, TrailOffset=50, uni-directional
            ratchet) UNCHANGED from V3.0.
          - New inputs: L1c_Ratio (default 0.7), Floor_Points
            (default 0). Both are Optimizer sweep dimensions
            (56 combos: 14 Ratio x 4 Floor). See spec Section 4.
          - Sanity case (L1c_Ratio = 999): Layer 1 * 999 always
            exceeds Layer 0; Layer 0 binds; behavior equivalent to
            V3.0 T200 baseline (regression test per spec Section
            4.2.1).
          - P3b Immediate Stop Guard updated to mirror the same
            L1_c + fallback logic (per spec Section 6.2). Both
            P3b and Frozen SL blocks use identical Bug-1 fix
            condition: (v_L1c_ready AND v_L1c_raw > 0).
          - Diagnostic Print at entry-bar freeze: logs
            Date, Time, EntryPrice, v_L1c_raw, v_L1c_ready,
            v_Layer1_dist, v_Layer0_dist, v_Frozen_SL_dist
            to v31_sl_log.txt. Post-hoc diagnosis for Optimizer
            anomaly investigation (New-4 recommendation).
          - Baseline: V3.0 T200 at commit 18facd4 (2026-07-23).
          - Spec: strategies/research/L1_v31/L1_v31_spec_20260724.md
          - Non-goal: NOT a smarter tightening layer, NOT a regime
            classifier, NOT a dynamic post-entry SL modification.

  STRATEGY LOGIC (V3.1):
    P2 Entry  : Close crosses above MA61 + ATR x Entry_Multiplier
    P3 Stop   : 4-Layer defense.
                Layer 0 (hard cap): MinList(Current_ATR * SL_Mult,
                                            Daily_ATR   * Cap_Mult)
                Layer 1 (primary) : MaxList(v_L1c_raw * L1c_Ratio,
                                            Floor_Points)
                                    Cold-start / L1_c=0 fallback:
                                    Current_ATR * SL_Multiplier
                Frozen SL distance = MinList(Layer 0, Layer 1),
                locked at entry. Frozen SL price = Entry - distance.
    P3b Guard : SetStopLoss (engine-level, active on entry bar).
                Distance mirrors P3 formula. SetStopContract basis.
    P4 Trail  : MA55 - TrailOffset, uni-directional ratchet (V3.0)
    P7 Guard  : Stop Profit - armed at +200 pts tick-based (V3.0 IOG),
                lock floor = Entry + peak x 45 pct, ratchets up only
    P5 v3     : Pre-holiday flat rule (block entries on tail bars,
                forced market exit from Holiday_Flat_Time)
    P6 Filter : Data3 Weekly OR filter (20MA / 60MA)
    P6 Settle : Monthly Settlement flat rule (3rd Wed 12:30 exit)
    Exit      : single stop at Max(P4 trail, P3 frozen, P7 lock)

  PERFORMANCE (V3.0 baseline reference, Excel Report 2026/07/02,
